A translate/dub target must be a language the source LACKS — the source already speaks the language it was recorded in. The context names each source's detected language when known — that signal is authoritative, trust it over inference; absent it, judge from the user's words / filename / prompt language. '中英双语' on a Chinese talk → target 'en', never 'zh' — translating Chinese into Chinese produces no English anywhere; the same request on an English keynote (detected language: en) → target 'zh'.
